  "id": "banded-single-leg-hip-thrust",
  "name": "Banded Single-Leg Hip Thrust",
  "definition": "A unilateral bench-supported hip thrust with one heel planted and a long band across the pelvis, its ends secured toward the floor by heavy dumbbells. The opposite knee stays lifted near a right angle while the working hip extends to neutral against increasing band tension. Band tension and anchor geometry are not quantified, so resistance is non-comparable. A mini band around the knees, bilateral thrust, floor glute bridge, and externally loaded barbell thrust remain outside this exact fixture.",
